+/*
+ * SWEET Adreno 618 (davinci / SM7150 / sdmmagpie) bring-up - Phase 0 / 0.5.
+ * Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one thread.
+ *
+ * LESSON (first boot, sweetgpu=1): a pure read of GPUCC/CX-misc HARD-FAULTS
+ * (external abort -> panic -> reset), because those blocks are clock-gated by
+ * gcc_gpu_cfg_ahb_clk which ABL leaves OFF under XNU - a gated register block
+ * aborts, it does not return 0xffffffff. So Phase 0 must first enable the GPU
+ * AHB/config clocks via GCC (always-accessible, clocks every live peripheral)
+ * BEFORE touching the GPU clock-controller window.
+ *
+ * Phase 0 (sweetgpu=1): read GCC GPU clock status (safe), enable the GPU
+ * config/AHB/NoC clocks, then read GPUCC offset 0 to prove MMIO reach. Does
+ * NOT touch the GPU CORE (0x5000000, GX domain, GMU-gated), votes no GX rail,
+ * loads no firmware. The QFPROM fuse block is NOT read (access-controlled).
+ *
+ * Phase 0.5 (sweetgpu=2): additionally one read-only TrustZone query,
+ * PAS_IS_SUPPORTED(pas-id 13) - "does TZ expose the GPU zap PAS service".
+ * No memory setup / image load / reset. An unrecognised SMC returns SMCCC
+ * NOT_SUPPORTED (x0=-1), it does not hang. See trustzone-pas-feasibility.md.
+ *
+ * Addresses from davinci-p-oss (gcc-sdmmagpie.c, sdmmagpie-gpu.dtsi):
+ *   GCC base 0x100000; gpu branches (offset within GCC): cfg_ahb 0x71004,
+ *   memnoc_gfx 0x7100c, snoc_dvm_gfx 0x71018, ddrss_gpu_axi 0x4452c (BIT0);
+ *   GPUCC 0x5090000/0x9000, chipid 0x06010800 (a618).
+ */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
